        {"type":"mol","smiles":"O=S(=O)(Cl)c1ccccc1"}
     ]
   }
 ]
}

But need to embed the second reaction as child of the first precursor? Actually hierarchical: root product -> reaction1 -> precursors. One of those precursors itself is a molecule that can be further broken down via reaction2. So we need nested children: The first precursor node should have its own children reaction. So structure:

root mol
 children: reaction1 node
   children: mol1 (which has its own children reaction2), mol2 (terminal)

Thus:

{
 "type":"mol",
 "smiles":"<target>",
 "children":[
   {
     "type":"reaction",
     "template_id": <id1>,
     "children":[
        {
          "type":"mol",
          "smiles":"Cc1ccc(NS(=O)(=O)c2ccc(/C=C/C(=O)O)cc2)cc1",
          "children":[
            {
              "type":"reaction",
              "template_id":41227,
              "children":[
                {"type":"mol","smiles":"Nc1ccc2c(c1)C(=O)c1ccccc1C2=O"},
                {"type":"mol","smiles":"O=S(=O)(Cl)c1ccccc1"}
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {"type":"mol","smiles":"Nc1ccc(cc1)N"}
     ]
   }
 ]
}

